{
  "case_id": "2024-24a884",
  "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Applicants",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Universal injunctions exceed the judicial power granted in Article III, which exists only to address the injury to the complaining party. They transgress the traditional bounds of equitable authority, and they create a host of practical problems."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: General Sauer, the -- these universal injunctions, as you say, have proliferated over the last three decades or so. Would you discuss, though, the origins of universal injunctions? In particular, I'm interested in sort of historical analogues or the historical pedigree, particularly the bill of peace that -- that was proffered by Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Applicants",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL SAUER: We are not claiming that because we're conceding that there could be a -- in an appropriate case, a Rule 23 class action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Applicants",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "court may issue -- the --the lower courts may issue injunctions that remediate the injuries to the plaintiffs that appear before them. Lower courts in appropriate cases may certify class actions --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is now fully briefed in the Ninth Circuit in Case Number 25-807, where we describe how that characterization of the holding of Wong Kim Ark and the other decisions is profoundly incorrect."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0011",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Article III context, that is the principle announced in Warth against Seldin, announced in Gill against Whitford, in Lewis against Casey, where this Court has said again and again: What we do in the Article III context is grant remedy that is tailored to -- grant remedies that are tailored to remove the injury to the complaining plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Applicants",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I disagree with that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0013",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Article III context, this Court said in Warth against Seldin, for example, that the Article III judicial power exists only to redress the injury to the complaining parties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0017",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Do you concede that the plaintiffs could bring a Rule 23, like the individual plaintiffs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what -- what do you say, though, to the suggestion, General, that in this particular case, those patchwork problems for, frankly, the government, as -- as well as for plaintiffs, justify broader relief?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do we need to reach the Article III question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How could it? If Article III and only prohibits injunctions that affect non-members or non-plaintiffs, how could Congress give a remedy like a class action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So, General, on this question of expedition, I mean, it -- it sort of depends on the government's own actions in a case like this one, where one can expect that there is not going to be a great deal of disagreement among the lower courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: How do you suggest we reach this case on the merits expeditiously?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: So the technical problem here seems to be class-wide relief without the district courts going through the steps to assess whether a class should be certified, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: This administration's practice or the longstanding practice of the federal government? And I'm not talking about in the Fourth Circuit are you going to respect a Second Circuit. I'm talking about within the Second Circuit. And can you say is that this administration's practice or a longstanding one?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But the government's done that in other cases too, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL SAUER: Yes. But also, more fundamentally, it illustrates that the very problem with these nationwide injunctions is they force -- they -- they -- they force this rushed, you know, fast-and-furious decisions on the merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: So, as far as I can tell, your bottom line seems to be that what you call universal injunctions give relief to nonparties without going through the necessary steps, which you identify in Rule 23. Do I have that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeremy M. Feigenbaum",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGENBAUM: So I do feel like something of an amicus to this question because nothing in my injunction rises or falls on this claim bucket."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you -- do you agree about the rigors of class certification?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Feigenbaum",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "States can't represent those individuals in class actions, nor would we try to. They can't represent us and you don't have classes of states. So the whole framework doesn't apply to state litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are -- are you telling us that we really can't decide the question that we asked to have briefing and argument on without taking a -- a peek at the merits?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 100,
        "start": 100
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The court of appeals gives it the back of the hand, and then the case comes immediately to us in the context of an emergency application."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 102,
        "start": 102
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you agree with me that they were not presented to the courts below?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 112,
        "start": 112
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: General, you had a chance to talk about your administrative costs and the workability problems that New Jersey"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 119,
        "start": 119
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court in -- in the Massachusetts case did actually do a very good job of this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Corkran (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I -- you know, again, I would put us in the complete relief bucket."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Corkran (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Rule 71 explicitly contemplates that and says, if a nonparty receives relief, they are entitled to enforce it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I understand General Sauer's proposal to be that we channel all of this through Rule 23."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 130,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: -- why can't you get putative class relief in a preliminary injunction or TRO posture?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Corkran (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 138,
        "start": 138
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It would eliminate the associational standing trade cases, you know, the cases brought by the Chamber of Commerce, the NRA, other associations that aren't suitable for class certification."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 151,
        "start": 151
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Justice Gorsuch? Justice Kavanaugh?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 153,
        "start": 153
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Ms. Corkran, I just have one question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Professor Pfander",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 157,
        "start": 157
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Professor Pfander's amicus brief is really helpful on that. He talks about the -- the patent laws."
    },
    {
